#!/usr/bin/env bash
# Every function's description and grants, in one place. Regenerates
# functions/<name>/<name>.json; never edit those by hand (bin/fnjson.py, as Roadmap's).
#   table   read        table:rw  + write rows        table:rwd  + delete rows
#   function:<name>     run it    workflow:<name>  start it    /folder:verbs   a folder
# A /me path needs no grant (and the importer refuses one): a function run as
# a person reaches their own files.
set -euo pipefail
cd "$(dirname "$0")/.."
f() { uv run --no-project python bin/fnjson.py "$@"; }
NEEDS="interviews_study interviews_proposal needs_you:rw"
f interviews_setup "User interviews' set-up as the person: check says where they stand (the team's product, contact rules, their Mail, Meetings and booking page, and what is missing); save picks or makes the team's product, keeps the contact rules and writes the memory block. Safe to run again." interviews_settings:rw product:rw mail_mailbox meetings_settings meetings_calendar booking_settings booking_page function:interviews_memory
f interviews_memory "Tells this Lemma's agents that User interviews is installed: its block in /memory/AGENTS.md and its guide at /memory/plugins/user-interviews.md, leaving the team's notes alone. Set-up runs it; safe to run again. remove takes both out." /memory:read,write
f interviews_sample_data "load: a made-up study (a reporting product, people at .example companies in every stage, one call's findings to review, three calls' findings kept) to look around with; its invites are only marked sent. clear: removes only what the sample made." product:rwd company:rwd company_domain:rwd deal:rwd feature:rwd feedback:rwd interviews_study:rwd interviews_person:rwd interviews_pasted:rwd interviews_finding:rwd interviews_proposal:rwd draft:rwd interviews_sample_row:rwd interviews_settings:rw mail_mailbox meetings_settings booking_settings needs_you:rw /interviews-sample:read,write,delete
f interviews_pool "Build or refresh one study's people (study_id): everyone the team knows from feedback, asks, deals, the member's own people and pasted lists who fits the study's filters, ranked (said something about its features, then a won or open deal, then recency), with why they fit, their best quote and the contact rules. Reads no mail or meeting text." interviews_study:rw interviews_person:rwd interviews_pasted interviews_settings feedback ask deal feature person person_handle people_person mail_mailbox
f interviews_fit "Who fits a study, read from its sentence around the interviews-fit-reader agent. brief: the sentence and the fields and values this Lemma holds. save: keeps filters on real fields, marks anything else as no data, writes fit_read and builds the pool." interviews_study:rw interviews_pasted feature deal function:interviews_pool
f interviews_invite "One invite for one person (person_id) around the interviews-inviter agent, as the member who will send it. brief: refuses a resting or opted-out person and a member with no mailbox or booking page, else the study, the person, the member's voice and booking link. save: a Mail draft (kind new, proposed); the person moves to drafted. Never sends." interviews_person:rw interviews_settings feature mail_mailbox mail_settings booking_settings draft:rw $NEEDS
f interviews_send "Send one invite (person_id), as the member pressing Send: saves their edits, approves the draft and has Mail send it from their mailbox. Sent: invited, and the contact rules start for them elsewhere. Not sent: stays drafted with the reason. A sample invite is only marked sent." interviews_person:rw interviews_study:rw interviews_settings draft:rw mail_mailbox function:mail_send_draft $NEEDS
f interviews_on_meeting "One of the member's meetings (meeting_id), from their own trigger: an invited person of a running study among its attendees, after the invite, is booked; a booked call's transcript or notes start the read." meeting meetings_work interviews_person:rw interviews_study workflow:interviews-read
f interviews_read "Read one call (person_id) around the interviews-reader agent, as the member who had it. brief: the document, the study's question and features, who spoke. save: keeps a proposal only when its quote is in the document word for word, with the minute from the nearest [m:ss], never the member's own lines; then their Today." interviews_person:rw interviews_proposal:rwd feature meetings_settings mail_settings $NEEDS /interviews-sample:read /meetings-sample:read
f interviews_keep "Keep or set aside one proposed finding (proposal_id; keep, undo; an edited point, feature_id or feature_new, kind, importance), as the interviewer. Kept: a feedback row by the contract's id (source interview or note, the call's source_id, at_seconds, heard_by them, processed), a suggested feature for a new name, and its place in the study." interviews_proposal:rw interviews_person:rw interviews_finding:rwd feedback:rw feature:rw product meeting interviews_settings interviews_sample_row:rw interviews_study needs_you:rw
f interviews_paste "A call's words no meeting brought (person_id, text, kind transcript or notes): a pasted transcript (Name: words, [m:ss] or VTT) or typed notes, kept in the member's own files, then read for findings." interviews_person:rw /interviews-sample:read,write workflow:interviews-read
f interviews_mark "Mark one person in a study (person_id, what): no_show (rests them for the no-show days), showed, declined, opted_out (never invited again), thanked or unthanked (a tick; nobody is paid), override (invite despite a rest, kept), skip, restore." interviews_person:rw interviews_settings $NEEDS
f interviews_findings "What one study (study_id) found, by feature: people with kept findings per feature ('4 of 6 people'), findings, blockers, Roadmap stage, a person-by-feature grid, what the last call changed, and one feature's quotes with their call and minute (feature_id). Its text is a ready answer." interviews_study interviews_finding interviews_person feedback feature
f interviews_daily "Each member's own morning run (and the app's refresh): bookings and documents a trigger missed, a nudge asked of Mail for an invite unanswered after the nudge days (in that invite's thread, once synced), and their Today: findings to review, did they show up, invites to send." interviews_person:rw interviews_settings meeting meetings_work draft message mail_thread:rw workflow:interviews-read $NEEDS
